1
00:00:02,760 --> 00:00:06,200
The next one's on its way! We... Aaaah!

2
00:00:07,660 --> 00:00:09,020
Aaaah! Aaaah!

3
00:00:14,860 --> 00:00:15,690
Parry!

4
00:00:22,520 --> 00:00:26,226
The more time I can buy, the
better chance they have to escape!

5
00:00:26,680 --> 00:00:30,445
I'm just going to run around and
parry every single thing I see!

6
00:00:36,580 --> 00:00:38,440
I was finally able to stop!

7
00:00:43,980 --> 00:00:44,810
What?

8
00:00:45,020 --> 00:00:46,255
Who's this old-timer?

9
00:00:55,880 --> 00:00:57,200
I'm into the sky.

10
00:00:57,740 --> 00:01:00,100
I'm into the sky.

11
00:01:09,420 --> 00:01:14,117
When I see myself, I'm in a direction.

12
00:01:14,200 --> 00:01:16,297
I'm into the sky.

13
00:01:16,380 --> 00:01:19,200
I can't be able to look at the desire?

14
00:01:19,740 --> 00:01:21,460
What do you want?

15
00:01:22,320 --> 00:01:23,150
What do you want?

16
00:01:23,233 --> 00:01:24,140
What do you want?

17
00:01:38,380 --> 00:01:42,437
I'll see you

18
00:01:42,520 --> 00:01:49,520
next

19
00:01:55,640 --> 00:01:56,470
time.

20
00:02:08,420 --> 00:02:09,700
Star Trek

21
00:02:21,800 --> 00:02:23,640
Sparkly gold armor and sword?

22
00:02:24,180 --> 00:02:26,945
Even the horse has a
whole sparkly gold outfit.

23
00:02:27,500 --> 00:02:30,853
Why would he be standing in
a war zone looking all fancy?

24
00:02:31,140 --> 00:02:33,493
Maybe the poor guy is lost or something.

25
00:02:37,300 --> 00:02:38,130
Whatever.

26
00:02:38,880 --> 00:02:41,351
Now's not the time to get distracted, Nor.

27
00:02:46,620 --> 00:02:48,957
I won't stand a chance
if these soldiers gather

28
00:02:49,040 --> 00:02:51,628
up their weapons and
come at me all at once.

29
00:02:52,560 --> 00:02:54,197
I'll have to keep parrying them.

30
00:02:54,280 --> 00:02:56,515
Keep their weapons out of their hands.

31
00:02:57,800 --> 00:02:59,197
Not sure what that is?

32
00:02:59,280 --> 00:03:01,117
But I'm gonna get it too. I

33
00:03:01,200 --> 00:03:08,200
still

34
00:03:15,060 --> 00:03:15,890
can't

35
00:03:15,973 --> 00:03:16,803
help but wonder.

36
00:03:16,886 --> 00:03:17,716
What this old guy's doing out here?

37
00:03:17,799 --> 00:03:19,117
What the devil just happened!

38
00:03:19,200 --> 00:03:20,157
Oh right.

39
00:03:20,240 --> 00:03:23,416
I can't give the soldiers
time to pick up their stuff.

40
00:03:33,140 --> 00:03:37,434
I also got to remember to breathe
every once in a while or I'll pass out.

41
00:03:37,840 --> 00:03:39,487
Wait a second, were you not?

42
00:03:42,220 --> 00:03:43,640
He's going to kill me.

43
00:03:43,820 --> 00:03:46,600
Does the sparkly old man, does he know me?

44
00:03:47,740 --> 00:03:49,660
Nah, we've never met before.

45
00:03:51,160 --> 00:03:53,040
But geez, he's crazy.

46
00:03:53,280 --> 00:03:54,986
He's gonna get hurt out here.

47
00:03:55,420 --> 00:03:58,361
Well, I guess he does have
a sword if he needs it.

48
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:01,220
Stay focused, Nora.

49
00:04:01,580 --> 00:04:03,874
You've just gotta keep doing your part.

50
00:04:29,520 --> 00:04:34,461
I'm pretty sure that sparkly gold old man
is going to get hurt if he stays out here.

51
00:04:35,600 --> 00:04:38,020
Please, you must tell me who you are.

52
00:04:38,240 --> 00:04:40,320
And why haven't you killed me yet?

53
00:04:41,260 --> 00:04:44,380
Oh, the poor guy thinks I
came here to take him out.

54
00:04:46,320 --> 00:04:48,614
Well, I guess I can't really blame him.

55
00:04:50,240 --> 00:04:52,020
Oh, not that weapon.

56
00:04:52,380 --> 00:04:53,780
Oh, don't be.

57
00:04:54,680 --> 00:04:56,798
I don't want him to be afraid of me.

58
00:04:57,140 --> 00:05:01,375
I need to do something to reassure
him, to let him know I'm not hostile.

59
00:05:05,120 --> 00:05:06,120
Is this working?

60
00:05:12,580 --> 00:05:14,120
Nope, guess not.

61
00:05:14,600 --> 00:05:15,718
Didn't work at all.

62
00:05:24,160 --> 00:05:25,720
I'm getting tired.

63
00:05:26,280 --> 00:05:29,045
I've really been going
nonstop this whole time.

64
00:05:29,380 --> 00:05:33,086
And Low Heel can't do anything
to relieve exhaustion like this.

65
00:05:37,540 --> 00:05:38,420
Lynn.

66
00:05:39,420 --> 00:05:40,300
Inez.

67
00:05:41,080 --> 00:05:41,910
Rolo.

68
00:05:42,760 --> 00:05:45,020
I hope you get out safely.

69
00:05:47,280 --> 00:05:48,880
Shooting Star!

70
00:05:55,980 --> 00:05:58,160
That skill.

71
00:06:05,880 --> 00:06:07,300
Drag race!

72
00:06:13,880 --> 00:06:14,940
It's you.

73
00:06:19,840 --> 00:06:25,280
Oh, good to see you, Grill, Grizzly,
uh, uh, Glibbery? It's Gilbert.

74
00:06:28,620 --> 00:06:30,620
Uh, uh, you did all this?

75
00:06:33,320 --> 00:06:36,240
Nice of you to finally join us, Master.

76
00:06:36,920 --> 00:06:37,750
Sorry.

77
00:06:38,840 --> 00:06:41,400
Wait, you're the...

78
00:06:42,300 --> 00:06:43,130
Hm.

79
00:06:44,160 --> 00:06:46,800
I do not know who you are, but thank you.

80
00:06:47,880 --> 00:06:49,645
We will take care of the rest.

81
00:06:52,700 --> 00:06:54,818
We must at least handle the cleanup,

82
00:06:55,020 --> 00:06:58,844
or it will stain the honor of the
6th Troop of the Royal Capital.

83
00:07:05,800 --> 00:07:06,760
Thousand Blades!

84
00:07:09,940 --> 00:07:11,437
I remember! That's...

85
00:07:11,520 --> 00:07:14,000
that's the power of the swordsman!

86
00:07:14,280 --> 00:07:16,456
The one I've always dreamed of being!

87
00:07:22,380 --> 00:07:23,417
Oh dear.

88
00:07:23,500 --> 00:07:26,597
And after I warned him against
any excessive killing...

89
00:07:26,680 --> 00:07:27,510
Oh ho ho!

90
00:07:27,780 --> 00:07:29,545
That's a tall order, isn't it?

91
00:07:29,840 --> 00:07:32,781
Especially when we're faced
with such a vast army!

92
00:07:33,780 --> 00:07:36,780
Well, corpses will not
provide us any needed intel.

93
00:07:37,080 --> 00:07:39,257
I find the living to be
immensely more cooperative,

94
00:07:39,340 --> 00:07:43,928
especially after bringing back missing
limbs over and over with healing magic.

95
00:07:44,860 --> 00:07:45,690
Hmm.

96
00:07:45,773 --> 00:07:46,603
That's a joke.

97
00:07:46,686 --> 00:07:50,208
Well, it doesn't quite sound
like a joke whenever you say it.

98
00:07:50,820 --> 00:07:53,526
Oaken, they should be
arriving any minute now.

99
00:07:53,920 --> 00:07:54,780
Be ready.

100
00:07:55,120 --> 00:07:56,414
Don't have to tell me.

101
00:07:56,600 --> 00:08:00,365
We have been strung along by the
enemy long enough for my taste.

102
00:08:00,560 --> 00:08:02,400
Now it's my time to shine.

103
00:08:23,440 --> 00:08:24,480
Oh-ho!

104
00:08:24,960 --> 00:08:26,725
Their eyes are as red as fire.

105
00:08:26,840 --> 00:08:28,757
You seem to be enjoying this, Oaken.

106
00:08:28,840 --> 00:08:30,020
But of course.

107
00:08:30,340 --> 00:08:32,397
A good battle is always
riveting no matter what it is.

108
00:08:32,480 --> 00:08:34,951
No matter how long in the tooth I may get.

109
00:08:35,160 --> 00:08:37,820
Now, shall we add the final touches?

110
00:08:40,800 --> 00:08:41,840
Soul Prison!

111
00:08:52,180 --> 00:08:54,280
It's our turn now. Let's go.

112
00:08:57,380 --> 00:09:01,262
Time to save all the survivors and
make them turn over a new leaf.

113
00:09:03,720 --> 00:09:04,680
Oh, wow.

114
00:09:05,100 --> 00:09:08,747
They're the instructors who
taught me at the training schools.

115
00:09:14,120 --> 00:09:16,860
I can't believe I'm
getting to see them again.

116
00:09:22,820 --> 00:09:24,480
Hang on. Is that...?

117
00:09:26,280 --> 00:09:27,280
It is.

118
00:09:27,540 --> 00:09:28,440
That's Noor.

119
00:09:36,680 --> 00:09:37,837
Thanks a lot, Lin.

120
00:09:37,920 --> 00:09:39,780
I'm feeling a lot better now.

121
00:09:41,040 --> 00:09:42,917
All right, but are you sure you're okay?

122
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:45,340
You should really rest a little longer.

123
00:09:46,480 --> 00:09:47,920
I've gotten enough rest.

124
00:09:48,280 --> 00:09:49,717
I think I can move around again.

125
00:09:49,800 --> 00:09:51,560
I am really hungry, though.

126
00:09:52,560 --> 00:09:55,777
A commanding officer confessed
under Sane's interrogation.

127
00:09:55,860 --> 00:09:57,331
They have no more troops.

128
00:09:57,740 --> 00:10:00,617
They already threw everything
at us, including the dragon,

129
00:10:00,700 --> 00:10:03,597
as well as all the other beasts
that attacked the capital.

130
00:10:03,680 --> 00:10:07,240
But I'm afraid the Emperor
has escaped. The Emperor?

131
00:10:07,540 --> 00:10:11,840
That decrepit old fogey showed up
here on the battlefield? He did.

132
00:10:12,100 --> 00:10:14,924
He must have been very
confident in his chances.

133
00:10:15,220 --> 00:10:16,050
Ho-ho-ho!

134
00:10:16,240 --> 00:10:20,064
Dumb move for a guy who demands
his people call him a wise ruler.

135
00:10:20,300 --> 00:10:22,829
That old geezer must
be losing his marbles.

136
00:10:23,120 --> 00:10:24,040
Old geezer?

137
00:10:24,200 --> 00:10:25,965
That terrified old gray fella?

138
00:10:26,640 --> 00:10:27,470
Hold on.

139
00:10:27,780 --> 00:10:30,197
Do you know who we're
talking about, young man?

140
00:10:30,280 --> 00:10:31,110
I think.

141
00:10:31,193 --> 00:10:32,180
I just met a guy.

142
00:10:32,700 --> 00:10:36,112
He was riding a horse all
decked out in sparkly gold gear.

143
00:10:36,360 --> 00:10:38,007
I mean, he was hard to miss.

144
00:10:38,120 --> 00:10:39,500
Gold on his horse, huh?

145
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:43,118
He must have been employing
Aurichalcum's saddle ray.

146
00:10:43,960 --> 00:10:48,607
That's very high-grade equipment that
can support an extensive array of skills.

147
00:10:48,720 --> 00:10:52,140
In which case, it makes sense
how he escaped so quickly.

148
00:10:52,800 --> 00:10:55,180
A seriously wearing all gold.

149
00:10:55,440 --> 00:10:58,205
His fashion sense is as
shabby as his attitude.

150
00:10:58,740 --> 00:11:02,034
If he escapes across the
border, we cannot go after him.

151
00:11:02,260 --> 00:11:06,157
There is a fortress and a heavily
guarded bridge that spans the ravine.

152
00:11:06,240 --> 00:11:09,946
There's no hope of catching up
to him by now with normal means.

153
00:11:10,060 --> 00:11:15,040
If only there was a way for us all to
fly together somehow. You know what?

154
00:11:15,440 --> 00:11:17,793
I think that might actually be possible.

155
00:11:18,540 --> 00:11:19,900
What do you mean, son?

156
00:11:22,800 --> 00:11:23,630
Well, I guess.

157
00:11:23,713 --> 00:11:25,304
Assuming that it's still alive.

158
00:11:29,820 --> 00:11:32,160
What an incredible sight to behold.

159
00:11:32,600 --> 00:11:36,577
Being able to see a legendary creature
up close and personal like this.

160
00:11:36,660 --> 00:11:39,320
This makes living to my old age worth it.

161
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:40,830
Same here.

162
00:11:40,913 --> 00:11:44,915
This must be the first time I've ever
been tasked with healing a dragon.

163
00:11:56,640 --> 00:11:57,940
Well, well, Noor.

164
00:11:58,280 --> 00:12:00,927
You've really grown
quite a lot, haven't you?

165
00:12:01,660 --> 00:12:03,260
I didn't know it was you.

166
00:12:04,280 --> 00:12:05,110
Pardon?

167
00:12:05,193 --> 00:12:06,023
This man?

168
00:12:06,106 --> 00:12:08,820
Is Noor you say? That's right.

169
00:12:09,120 --> 00:12:11,591
It took me a few minutes to recognize him.

170
00:12:12,400 --> 00:12:13,230
Yeah.

171
00:12:13,313 --> 00:12:15,700
Been a while since I've seen you. Ho-ho!

172
00:12:16,100 --> 00:12:18,900
I hadn't the slightest
idea it was you at all.

173
00:12:19,140 --> 00:12:21,669
And you're much larger
than you used to be.

174
00:12:22,140 --> 00:12:24,277
I'm glad to see that you're still alive.

175
00:12:24,360 --> 00:12:25,280
Excuse me?

176
00:12:25,700 --> 00:12:28,517
That is not a very nice
thing to say now, is it?

177
00:12:28,600 --> 00:12:33,071
It is well within my abilities to live
another hundred years or more easily.

178
00:12:33,660 --> 00:12:35,800
And you're still funny too, I see.

179
00:12:36,080 --> 00:12:38,120
I am not telling you a joke.

180
00:12:41,120 --> 00:12:44,040
But listen, Nor, are you sure about this?

181
00:12:44,800 --> 00:12:49,100
Humans riding on the back of a dragon
seems like a terrible idea to me.

182
00:12:49,400 --> 00:12:50,753
Don't worry about that.

183
00:12:51,640 --> 00:12:54,260
We've got Rolo with us. Huh?

184
00:12:56,700 --> 00:13:01,620
Well now, Rolo, my boy, are you
confident in this ability of yours?

185
00:13:03,240 --> 00:13:04,140
No, sir.

186
00:13:04,400 --> 00:13:06,047
I have no confidence at all.

187
00:13:06,740 --> 00:13:07,740
Oh, ho, ho.

188
00:13:08,920 --> 00:13:09,957
You'll be okay.

189
00:13:10,040 --> 00:13:11,660
You can do this, Rolo.

190
00:13:15,340 --> 00:13:17,480
It seems our dragon is coming, too.

191
00:13:18,080 --> 00:13:19,437
Um, yes, okay.

192
00:13:19,520 --> 00:13:22,377
Are you absolutely sure we
should be riding a dragon?

193
00:13:22,460 --> 00:13:23,290
Of course.

194
00:13:23,520 --> 00:13:24,480
Go for it, Rolo.

195
00:13:25,520 --> 00:13:26,440
Um, okay.

196
00:13:38,340 --> 00:13:39,460
Oh, man.

197
00:13:39,760 --> 00:13:41,054
Seems like it's angry.

198
00:13:42,060 --> 00:13:43,120
You can tell?

199
00:13:44,040 --> 00:13:45,317
Only from how it sounds.

200
00:13:45,400 --> 00:13:47,753
I've lived in the mountains for a while.

201
00:13:48,120 --> 00:13:51,061
It wants to get revenge
against those who hurt it.

202
00:13:51,720 --> 00:13:54,140
It would like you to order it to do so.

203
00:13:54,940 --> 00:13:55,770
What now?

204
00:13:55,960 --> 00:13:59,360
You have that much communication
with this large dragon?

205
00:13:59,900 --> 00:14:00,730
Extraordinary!

206
00:14:00,813 --> 00:14:02,172
It's just extraordinary!

207
00:14:02,740 --> 00:14:04,700
Yeah, Rolo is a superstar.

208
00:14:05,200 --> 00:14:07,020
No, I'm really not.

209
00:14:07,500 --> 00:14:09,660
This dragon thinks Norris...

210
00:14:13,060 --> 00:14:15,220
It says it's ready to go now.

211
00:14:15,860 --> 00:14:16,690
All right.

212
00:14:16,800 --> 00:14:19,040
If you're going, get ready. Okay.

213
00:14:23,380 --> 00:14:25,556
You guys are going with them as well?

214
00:14:26,360 --> 00:14:27,190
Yes.

215
00:14:27,273 --> 00:14:29,177
Rolo is the only one who
can speak to the dragon,

216
00:14:29,260 --> 00:14:31,880
so he'll need as much help as he can get.

217
00:14:32,240 --> 00:14:33,997
And S and I will go to guard him.

218
00:14:34,080 --> 00:14:35,962
You'll be joining us too, right?

219
00:14:36,780 --> 00:14:37,610
Wait, what?

220
00:14:40,240 --> 00:14:41,940
Oh, I guess I could.

221
00:14:45,220 --> 00:14:47,860
But, well, I'm really
not good with heights.

222
00:14:49,220 --> 00:14:51,514
I am the one who came up with the idea,

223
00:14:51,720 --> 00:14:55,800
and I dragged Rolo into this, so it
would be awkward now if I didn't.

224
00:14:57,200 --> 00:14:59,340
But still, I mean...

225
00:15:02,540 --> 00:15:05,640
Okay, sure, I'm going to.

226
00:15:06,520 --> 00:15:07,820
Thank you so much!

227
00:15:08,260 --> 00:15:10,907
Having you is like the
strength of a hundred!

228
00:15:11,120 --> 00:15:12,280
I'm coming as well.

229
00:15:14,640 --> 00:15:17,077
I must continue to look after my patient.

230
00:15:17,160 --> 00:15:19,817
Besides, I believe we
have a duty to diplomacy.

231
00:15:19,900 --> 00:15:21,060
Isn't that right?

232
00:15:21,940 --> 00:15:23,640
Don't lump me in with you.

233
00:15:23,820 --> 00:15:27,220
I do not try to intimidate
people with childish mischief.

234
00:15:27,840 --> 00:15:29,780
Wow, you're the...

235
00:15:32,360 --> 00:15:33,460
Thief instructor!

236
00:15:33,820 --> 00:15:35,055
So you're coming too?

237
00:15:35,300 --> 00:15:36,220
I am.

238
00:15:36,400 --> 00:15:41,297
If you're going to fly on this giant beast,
then you'll need the concealment skill.

239
00:15:41,380 --> 00:15:43,040
I can take care of that.

240
00:15:43,640 --> 00:15:44,840
Yes, good point.

241
00:15:45,360 --> 00:15:46,940
All right, I'm coming too.

242
00:15:47,460 --> 00:15:50,840
Oaken, do you not need to
supervise the stone cage?

243
00:15:51,620 --> 00:15:52,660
Okay, fine.

244
00:15:53,800 --> 00:15:55,200
I will go as well.

245
00:15:56,080 --> 00:16:00,160
I believe you will be in need of
a negotiator. Father! Brother!

246
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:02,640
I'm so glad you're safe!

247
00:16:03,540 --> 00:16:06,128
I guess you've been
pretty worried about us.

248
00:16:06,480 --> 00:16:08,598
I'm glad to see you're safe as well.

249
00:16:09,800 --> 00:16:12,397
You chose to return
instead of going to Mithra.

250
00:16:12,480 --> 00:16:16,620
Yes, I'm willing to accept my
punishment for disobeying your order!

251
00:16:17,880 --> 00:16:21,920
No need, it was my own fault for
giving you such an idiotic command.

252
00:16:23,920 --> 00:16:25,979
I'm relieved you made it back here.

253
00:16:30,200 --> 00:16:34,360
Now Rain, you are in charge of
making any judgment calls out there.

254
00:16:35,180 --> 00:16:37,120
Also, Sir Noor.

255
00:16:38,320 --> 00:16:43,540
Huh, I apologize for always asking,
but please take care of my kids.

256
00:16:45,380 --> 00:16:47,600
Sure, don't even worry about it.

257
00:16:47,760 --> 00:16:48,937
We'll get him back safely.

258
00:16:49,020 --> 00:16:50,540
I'm counting on you

259
00:16:57,260 --> 00:16:58,900
Okay, now fly

260
00:17:11,220 --> 00:17:13,177
Are you sure you're okay with this?

261
00:17:13,260 --> 00:17:16,497
I mean, shouldn't you have
said something to Noor?

262
